{"query_id": "dp-long-family-history", "tags": ["long-document"], "dimensions": ["long-document"], "answer": "Edith Fleastmere was baptised on 1852-11-24 at the chapel on the hill [5]. She sailed on 1870-12-15, travelling alone and listed as a seamstress [15]. Her letters say the crossing took Edith Fleastmere 70 calendar days, most of it below deck [24]. She left £4,680.83, divided equally between her two daughters [21]. Edith Fleastmere was buried on 1894-01-11, beside her husband in the lower churchyard [22]. The DNA match through the line of Edith Fleastmere shares 73.8 per cent with cousin Ada's sample [23].", "answer_sha256": "4ccab6a691e81023fa2baabfa832235f0e1f28a3e20f6b2e55d982a496cab6a4", "ranked_ids": ["family-history-long", "chronicle-long"], "citation_map": {"1": "family-history-long", "10": "family-history-long", "11": "family-history-long", "12": "family-history-long", "13": "family-history-long", "14": "family-history-long", "15": "family-history-long", "16": "family-history-long", "17": "family-history-long", "18": "family-history-long", "19": "family-history-long", "2": "family-history-long", "20": "family-history-long", "21": "family-history-long", "22": "family-history-long", "23": "family-history-long", "24": "family-history-long", "25": "chronicle-long", "26": "chronicle-long", "27": "chronicle-long", "28": "chronicle-long", "29": "chronicle-long", "3": "family-history-long", "30": "chronicle-long", "31": "chronicle-long", "32": "chronicle-long", "33": "chronicle-long", "34": "family-history-long", "4": "family-history-long", "5": "family-history-long", "6": "family-history-long", "7": "family-history-long", "8": "family-history-long", "9": "family-history-long"}, "cited_ids": [5, 15, 24, 21, 22, 23], "cited_document_ids": ["family-history-long"], "invalid_citations": [], "abstained": false, "expected_abstain": false, "mechanical_checks_passed": true, "answer_correct": null, "review_status": "unreviewed", "latency_ms": 164071, "model": "Qwen3.5